      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Rat were exposed to 80% nitrous oxide in oxygen for 1 and 18 h. Met-enkephalin levels in the dorsal raphé, medial thalamus, periaqueductal grey, raphé magnus and locus coeruleus were measured by radioimmunoassay in control and treated animals. There was no change in Met-enkephalin levels at either time point in any of the brain areas examined."},
